<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Fresh protests over housing flare in Spain after lawmakers reject relief measures</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc89d4459f2ca8cd0012e75729b31b282d16a27bdb255874de985c4da412d027</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T13:20:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures--704e7b8d4986.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched in Madrid and other cities in Spain on Saturday to demand affordable housing, fuelled by anger at lawmakers who narrowly rejected measures put forward by the government of Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to strengthen protection for tenants.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes another major bridge across Kyiv's Dnipro river</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e70e0fc019afcbac1ad28d7dddc7790397f371d5657cdae577743f547afba30c</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv--263369bf48e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Kyiv's Northern Bridge across the Dnipro river was hit by a Russian air attack, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said Saturday, amid an escalation in strikes ​on ‌infrastructure in the Ukrainian capital. The attack comes a day after the city's Southern Bridge was hit by several strikes that officials said were "tearing Kyiv apart".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We have to close defence gaps urgently': EU Parliament Foreign Affairs Committee chief McAllister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b9982905a51eebb06b0ab3ac883cbdb88047c891789ab6715e08d1e7ea984ad</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:57:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-we-have-to-close-defence-gaps-urgently-eu-parliament-foreign-affairs-committee-chief-mcalli--0a159ccef672.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-we-have-to-close-defence-gaps-urgently-eu-parliament-foreign-affairs-committee-chief-mcallister" /><summary type="html">We sit down with David McAllister, the chair of the European Parliament’s Foreign Affairs Committee. He talks to us about the security threats facing Europe, and what defence gaps the EU urgently needs to close. For McAllister, the EU is "not at war with the Russian Federation, but we are no longer at peace with Russia". He also believes that the EU is not, as yet, capable of making sovereign decisions in certain areas of defence "because we are too dependent on US capabilities."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish lawmakers vote down affordable housing bills in blow to Sanchez’s government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7eb994d8881526de1adc5b6fa0f613251cdb3d345d57daa971cb26a20beeb962</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:12:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-spanish-lawmakers-vote-down-affordable-housing-bills-in-blow-to-sanchez-s-government--f124c72c5cdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-spanish-lawmakers-vote-down-affordable-housing-bills-in-blow-to-sanchez-s-government" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators protesting against Spain's housing crisis reacted with fury on Friday after the country's parliament rejected two bills put forward by the government that centre-left Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez hoped would address their concerns. Rents have doubled over the past decade, with average prices now almost equivalent to the average young person's monthly salary.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>A grim winter ahead? EU states asked to prepare gas and electricity savings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a941adb8f12bad9d2f01f4f30a03811e101be4998c1f054bc237b85d4f7ca7d9</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:10:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-a-grim-winter-ahead-eu-states-asked-to-prepare-gas-and-electricity-savings--d86d963689c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-a-grim-winter-ahead-eu-states-asked-to-prepare-gas-and-electricity-savings" /><summary type="html">Alarm bells are ringing about fuel prices across the EU. The average cost of diesel per litre is well above €2, whereas in October of last year it was around €1.50. Even before this latest spike, the cost of living was already biting, and it seems that the conflict in the Middle East is not going to give Europeans much respite as the winter draws closer. We review what EU member states have done to cushion the blow of rising energy prices for ordinary people, and whether those measures have been effective.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>G7 members will release 100 million barrels of diesel after US threatens export ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6bf3d354a5f94f40a3ab40cecc8ad09d4a053361a974d5e58e786c3cdbf3b46</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:15:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-eu-fully-rejects-us-threat-to-ban-diesel-exports-unless-bloc-releases-more-fuel-stocks--df4aae889a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-eu-fully-rejects-us-threat-to-ban-diesel-exports-unless-bloc-releases-more-fuel-stocks" /><summary type="html">Members of the Group of Seven bloc of highly industrialised economies on Friday agreed to release 100 million barrels of diesel and crude oil from their reserves over four months, averting a potential US ban on diesel exports. The European Union had earlier pushed back against Washington's threat, with an EU official saying the 27-member bloc “fully” rejected the move.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>As Europe's balance of power shifts eastward, France &amp; Spain seek to 'reinforce their own positions'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e787727e1dfb92981c25244677be9ff6d509cf8f784886c27a63665abf0f2eb4</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:49:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-as-europe-s-balance-of-power-shifts-eastward-france-spain-seek-to-reinforce-their-own-posit--c379b49194e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-as-europe-s-balance-of-power-shifts-eastward-france-spain-seek-to-reinforce-their-own-positions-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Carlos Mascarell Vilar, political scientist based in Spain. From his own perspective, Emmanuel Macron's visit to Spain needs to be understood by European power, political legacy, and geoeconomics. France and Spain are seeking to reinforce their bilateral relationship at a moment when the balance of power within Europe is changing rapidly, particularly with the growing importance of countries in the east such as Poland. For Macron, strengthening the Madrid-Paris axis is also part of a broader effort to advance European defence and strategic sovereignty.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia is ‘tearing Kyiv apart’, mayor says, as Moscow’s bombing brings traffic to a halt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc5ab9cc59a66c9147a7277736f2d0e2152f9b2e88e61b8a10471983edda7d6d</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T05:30:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-live-russia-hits-kyiv-s-southern-bridge-as-moscow-continues-to-pound-capital--530c711e233a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-live-russia-hits-kyiv-s-southern-bridge-as-moscow-continues-to-pound-capital" /><summary type="html">Russia is “tearing Kyiv apart”, the city’s Mayor Vitali Klitschko said on Friday, as Russia pummelled key infrastructure across the Ukrainian capital. Russian drones have pummelled Kyiv’s Southern Bridge, forcing authorities to close traffic on it. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US presses Europe to release diesel reserves 'immediately' as Trump threatens export ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3910ae3bfe0ec133849fd2dddffd26c4fe9ab38440d171ba342c1f822e04fd1</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:08:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-us-europe-diesel-reserves-fuel-prices--5176cf1419b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-us-europe-diesel-reserves-fuel-prices" /><summary type="html">The United States on Thursday urged European allies to release strategic diesel reserves immediately to curb prices driven higher by the US war on Iran. EU states will discuss a coordinated response on Friday, as Washington increases pressure following US President Donald Trump's suggestion that he could ban US diesel exports.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest dual UK-Iranian national over Fairford air base incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:611e018c4523646d86966213a3d54cc6ce8e14b809ea03b6f3c1fa5312dddf81</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T19:40:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident--eddc8f085ba4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident" /><summary type="html">British police on Thursday arrested a British-Iranian dual national in connection with the security incident at the Fairford airbase Wednesday. Five other men initially arrested over the incidence were later released without charge on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>A blessing or a curse? New Caledonia's dwindling nickel industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d488f4aa4453bc6856c23e670f7d333f8135fe23cdcefd5a1359d6233da4d82</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry--cc6e1bce2bc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry" /><summary type="html">This Thursday October 1, the French government is holding a summit aimed at attracting investors and revitalising wealth creation in France's overseas territories. Among the assets Paris wants to highlight is New Caledonian nickel. But the industry has been severely weakened by the political deadlock and tensions that have rocked the archipelago in recent years.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches major attack on Ukraine’s energy grid, causing power cuts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25784eec5440a43b9fc0e8d2f4c2ffbdfd85b1f5e2f0ce1b8fb4a7e65ca836ec</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T02:21:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-energy-grid-causing-power-cuts--006e908b4816.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-energy-grid-causing-power-cuts" /><summary type="html">Russia launched its heaviest combined assault on Ukraine’s energy infrastructure in months on Wednesday, killing seven people and triggering emergency power cuts in Kyiv and nearby regions. The strikes came as officials warned of a difficult winter amid Russian attacks on Ukraine’s power and heating infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c248e37ed5d2719fde459bebeca44cf4528381dd34fbac5bf62bf3b7db03c0bf</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T21:08:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260930-uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu--c4eec8c6baf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260930-uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table on Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham reopens divisive debate on rejoining EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5bae2fa6109dd55398de962fc4177f959bb5d61d365d6bc0b79124b8a57cc38</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T20:55:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu--23aa3f379bb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-reopens-divisive-debate-on-rejoining-eu" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham put the idea of Britain rejoining the EU on the table on Wednesday, breaking a taboo for a UK prime minister and reopening the divisive Brexit debate. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Catherine Barnard, Professor of European Law at the University of Cambridge, says that Burnham "is sending the message that actually it's been pretty cold being on the outside of the EU so we're now looking at the alternatives".</summary></entry><entry><title>British PM alleges there are 'strong indications' Iran was involved in Fairford airbase incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d07636749eab72d1f420ed6e2b680cfca9dd8aadb4495cddc0802789d4fa307</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incid--08fbaf5d3af6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-british-pm-alleges-there-are-strong-indications-iran-was-involved-in-fairford-airbase-incident" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Wednesday insisted that there were "strong indications" that Tehran was involved in a security incident on Sunday near an airbase in England that the US military uses in its war against Iran. The British government has still not explained the nature of the incident – in which five British men were arrested only to be later released on bail – and no explosives were found at the scene.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK-France 'one in, one out' migrant exchange deal is scrapped</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49f94abcb1c54a9f3eda305b3767ac465c92066b7c227abae43560fdc69b86b5</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:12:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped--b0a81c404ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-uk-france-one-in-one-out-migrant-exchange-deal-is-scrapped" /><summary type="html">A British-French agreement aimed at reducing the number of people trying to cross the English Channel in small boats has been scrapped, London said Wednesday. The pilot programme was intended to break the business model of "people smugglers" by exchanging undocumented migrants who had made the crossing for people who legally applied for asylum.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron says UK’s return to EU would be ‘excellent news’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:501e9890d0f2d096a0df59936a8d13ac7a0d1175f28d2e1b45332c8df9c12ec2</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T11:49:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-macron-sanchez-hold-joint-press-conference-during-french-president-s-spain-visit--5a73e2256a58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-macron-sanchez-hold-joint-press-conference-during-french-president-s-spain-visit" /><summary type="html">Speaking alongside Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Wednesday, French President Emmanuel Macron said that it would be "a good decision" if the UK decided to rejoin the European Union. The two leaders met at the Moncloa Palace in Madrid on the second day of Macron's two-day state visit to Spain.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine’s grid operator orders emergency power cuts in Kyiv after Russian strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd1b2844993e084e775ed88ff9321c6a7ddb0fdd43b9e1f8519f37542dafe559</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T05:35:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv--16599397238f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-several-people-killed-as-russia-launches-new-round-of-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's main energy provider DTEK said it had made emergency power cuts in Kyiv as directed by the national grid operator after Russia hit the country's infrastructure in a wave of deadly drone and missile strikes. At least seven people, including a 14-year-old child, were killed in the attacks, Ukrainian authorities said. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Mystery over UK airbase scare as police find petrol but no explosives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d24f898f5487722c901dff68674ca615cf1cd2fc46d9d0f91a58961d3f0f21f8</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T19:05:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives--1845b2e97bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-mystery-over-uk-airbase-scare-as-police-find-quantity-of-petrol-but-no-explosives" /><summary type="html">Britain's counter-terrorism police said ​on Tuesday that no improvised explosive devices had been found as part of an ​investigation ‌into a suspected plot targeting ⁠a British airbase used by US forces to ‌strike Iran, deepening uncertainty over the incident a day after five UK-based suspects were released on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham sets out 'new path' for Britain, vows to seek consensus on ties with EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d92184e0d51ce2090898af277410c410b58d17bb7fcb4cefdfe92ef3a4b820e</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T17:54:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu--7d1bd2026ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-burnham-sets-out-new-path-for-britain-vows-to-seek-consensus-on-ties-with-eu" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham pledged Tuesday to give Britain "a new social contract for the 21st century", reform the country's electoral system and build consensus on a new relationship with the European Union as he set out a long-term vision to tackle the UK's woes in his first speech as leader at the annual Labour party conference.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Putin's goal is to prolong his power in Russia': Journalist Roman Badanin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:999083c66e05d61daa428d7d997ef20a9ed1db02e93d12be1f0031d7a2cd2654</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T12:46:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260929-putin-s-goal-is-to-prolong-his-power-in-russia-journalist-roman-badanin--91a3d314be95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260929-putin-s-goal-is-to-prolong-his-power-in-russia-journalist-roman-badanin" /><summary type="html">A journalist who has spent more than 20 years investigating Russian leader Vladimir Putin and who is recognised as perhaps Russia's finest investigative journalist has told FRANCE 24 that Putin's aim with the war in Ukraine is simply to prolong his power inside Russia. Roman Badanin has just published a book, "Le Tsar en personne" or "The Tsar in person" which delves into exactly how Putin's mind works. Badanin says Putin acts like a gang member, and his attitude is that "if you beat me, I will beat you even harder". The book is so far out in Russian and French, with an English version to follow. He spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes two Kyiv data centres, cargo vessels in the Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35bed545e522f22cb4937fb3368bfa170d8a2f61801583f4fdcd1a74536d4dcf</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-russia-strikes-two-kyiv-data-centres-cargo-vessels-in-the-black-sea--a01e81e5bcd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-russia-strikes-two-kyiv-data-centres-cargo-vessels-in-the-black-sea" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that Russia launched a wave of overnight strikes across Ukraine, hitting two foreign-flagged vessels in the Black Sea and targets in Kyiv. The strikes come as Russia ramps up its pressure campaign intended to make Ukraine buckle under near-constant bombardment of its capital and other cities.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump 'surprised' UK granted bail to suspects in alleged airbase terror plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33cc1f26b873550cfac008e31f5d5e1460a095de75fe38e6c4acd7c43ac164fd</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T09:12:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-trump-surprised-uk-granted-bail-to-suspects-alleged-airbase-terror-plot--d79f276d3721.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260929-trump-surprised-uk-granted-bail-to-suspects-alleged-airbase-terror-plot" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Monday he was “surprised” British police released on bail five men arrested on suspicion of a plot to attack a UK airbase. Trump added the case “might be” linked to Iran, since the base has been used by US bombers to target Iran since March.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Class sizes of more than 36 people': School protests continue in Paris and beyond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ae6f4c7b914e069f430db55892548e8c364b4665e999f2985d115cdbb2e220c</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T07:59:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-class-sizes-of-more-than-36-people-student-protests-continue-in-paris-and-beyond-1--b5e875098054.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260929-class-sizes-of-more-than-36-people-student-protests-continue-in-paris-and-beyond-1" /><summary type="html">Teenagers in France have been blockading their schools and demonstrating since last week to protest a string of grievances. Standing in front of the Lycée Hélène Boucher, FRANCE 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan said students there said there were "class sizes of more than 36 people". Click on the video for more.</summary></entry><entry><title>87-year-old Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked protests to return home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520874ea2675a1b2bfb5425417bc8383d665b910665f4de11566d39f90d9024c</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T22:34:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-evicted-spanish-pensioner-to-return-home-after-housing-protest-deal-spain-madrid--1f3eaf89a642.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260928-evicted-spanish-pensioner-to-return-home-after-housing-protest-deal-spain-madrid" /><summary type="html">An 87-year-old Madrid pensioner whose eviction became a rallying point for Spain’s housing protests will be able to return home after reaching a deal with the property’s owners, her lawyer said Monday. The agreement comes as demonstrations across the country pile pressure on Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez’s government to address soaring rents, a shortage of affordable homes and weak tenant protections.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Expert says UK air base plot 'fits into a very intense pattern we've been seeing in past two months'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc357b3c8a3c31a9ae40b960a9d26c114a87ccc857f70350d9da62fc14ecb510</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T21:25:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260928-expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two---1fae47fd2b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260928-expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months" /><summary type="html">British police said on Monday that five men arrested near an air base used by the United States were released on bail, as officers probed whether a "foreign state" could be involved in a suspected bomb plot. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Yan Saint-Pierre, CEO of Modern Security Consulting Group, explains that many of the hybrid warfare cases seen recently "involve local nationals, this is not about exporting terror", adding that foreign actors aim to have "as many layers as possible to complicate any investigation and accurate denunciation of culprits".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Expert says UK air base plot 'fits into a very intense pattern we've been seeing in past two months'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:280e9e11d95641d82d2968d544a6b75080a79363fd97f13894ffaf170ba3518b</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T21:23:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months--4b79d9d157f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/expert-says-uk-airbase-plot-fits-into-a-very-intense-pattern-we-ve-been-seeing-in-past-two-months" /><summary type="html">British police said on Monday that five men arrested near an air base used by the United States were released on bail, as officers probed whether a "foreign state" could be involved in a suspected bomb plot. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Monte Francis, Yan Saint-Pierre, CEO of Modern Security Consulting Group, explains that many of the hybrid warfare cases seen recently "involve local nationals, this is not about exporting terror", adding that foreign actors aim to have "as many layers as possible to complicate any investigation and accurate denunciation of culprits".</summary></entry><entry><title>RAF Fairford: AI-enhanced photos of suspects fuel false claims about their religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6edb4a0d957db9d36e4e04364a3b470b8c96d40e0db7fa967d7adcde70614d5d</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T20:55:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/raf-fairford-ai-enhanced-photos-of-suspects-fuel-false-claims-about-their-religion-1--bb298c51157b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/raf-fairford-ai-enhanced-photos-of-suspects-fuel-false-claims-about-their-religion-1" /><summary type="html">Five men arrested over a suspected bomb plot at RAF Fairford have been released on bail as investigations continue. Meanwhile, AI-enhanced images purporting to show their faces have gone viral, with some users claiming this "proves" the men are Muslim. SynthID confirms the sharpened images were created using OpenAI tools, meaning the AI has suggested different facial features. UK police have not disclosed any names or religion, only that the men are all British nationals. Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian arms producers warn competitive edge eroding due to stringent export licence rules</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e77a6ec220f68261d7ea626b3339d56f4f34a138791d9bfd0a62cf805a393337</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T19:28:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-arms-producers-warn-competitive-edge-eroding-due-to-stringent-export-licence-rules--7f0830981503.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-arms-producers-warn-competitive-edge-eroding-due-to-stringent-export-licence-rules" /><summary type="html">Russian drones struck Ukraine's National Academy of Sciences in the historic heart of Kyiv on Monday, in the latest deadly daytime attack on the capital. Volodymyr Zelensky has long been pleading with Ukraine’s allies for more military aid to fend off Russia. But Ukrainian weapons producers say the country could be bringing in significant revenue of its own, if only they were allowed to export their products. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leo the moderate? Pope in France defends EU values</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e6c4dbf8daab6dbe6462a56db10f0bd1d4253044ea9427e5e8d395c5526fe49</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:31:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T18:49:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260928-leo-the-moderate-pope-in-france-defends-eu-values--553ee529b6c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260928-leo-the-moderate-pope-in-france-defends-eu-values" /><summary type="html">There's a new pope in town and he's got very different ideas on what France's far right calls the defense of Christian civilisation. Leo XIV is concluding his trip to France in the eastern city of Metz, which is closely associated with a founding father of present-day European federalism, Robert Schuman. There, the head of the world's largest organised religion proudly stated that Europe's roots are Christian, dating back to the Romans, all the while hailing an EU model that transcends "us versus them" ideology and brushes aside "might is right" in favour of human rights and international law.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry></feed>
